    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d726">

                <pb facs="0792" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/10–3144:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-07T00:00:00-04:00">November 7,
                            1944—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9326. From Department and FEA. Bern’s 7245, October 31 to Department. In the
                    event of an unsatisfactory reply (foreshadowed by Pilet-Golaz remarks) by the
                    Swiss Federal Council to our <hi rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> of October 31
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">30?</hi>], we feel formal withdrawal to our joint
                    offer of supplies should be made without delay in order to protect our future
                    position.</p>
                <p>You are requested to approach MEW at once to ascertain their views.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Bern as Department’s 3787. [Department and FEA.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
